https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iYYRH4apXDo  (Capo 0)

TIP:  If transposing play the root of the transposed (Gadd) and add the 5th note as needed.

TIP:  (Fmaj7) is just (F) without the 1st string.

TIP:  In the first two verses you can play (C) instead of (C/G) - just gives a little extra bass.  In the last verse you can play (C) and (G) and skip the add chords - just adds a little treble.

TIP:  (Fm) will always follow (F) so to move from the (F) to the (Fm) just sneak your index finger up a string to barre the lower three strings of the 1st fret while lifting off the middle finger.

TIP:  The instrumental bridge is a little tricky because it’s played so fast.

TIP:  At the end of the first verse end with strinking the |D7| once and then twizzle the top three or four strings (back and forth steadily) focusing on the open 4th string.

 
